Account Director Enterprise (DC) &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations are London, Berlin, Frankfurt, Munich and Hanover; with domestic and occasional international travel as required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driven by the rapid digital transformation of businesses across Europe, demand for high-capacity, reliable connectivity from Enterprise customers continues to grow. Thanks to our continued investment in the development of European fibre networks, euNetworks is a leader in Data Centre to Data Centre connectivity, supporting Hyperscale, Enterprise, Content and Wholesale customers across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Sales Director Data Centres you will play a key role in driving new business growth across the Enterprise market. You will do this by partnering, &#39;selling with&#39; with the sales teams of our DC customers to develop connectivity solutions for their DC tenants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in an experienced team, you will have the opportunity to develop and close large-scale European network opportunities (100G/400G) with Enterprise organisations that require high-performance connectivity across multiple locations. While you will also support the development of a small number of existing accounts, the primary focus of this role is building pipeline, acquiring new logos and expanding euNetworks’ presence within the Enterprise sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the support of our Sales Engineering team, with multiple engineers and additional account support available. You will also work closely with our Network Development, Digital Enablement and Product teams to shape solutions that meet customer needs and drive successful outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, target and win new Enterprise customers, building a strong pipeline of opportunities across the Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute new business sales strategies to expand euNetworks’ presence in the Enterprise market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders within prospective customer organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive opportunities from initial engagement through contract signature, meeting or exceeding sales and revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong understanding of the Enterprise connectivity market, identifying trends, potential customers and new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network at industry events, customer meetings and campaigns to generate leads and strengthen euNetworks’ market presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Sales Engineering and Product teams to develop technically and commercially viable solutions for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with commercial and finance teams to develop strong business cases and proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and growth of selected existing accounts, identifying opportunities for upselling and cross-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage sales activity and pipeline through Salesforce.com, ensuring accurate reporting and data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we want from you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant sales experience within Telecoms, Connectivity, Infrastructure or Technology markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong new business development experience, with a proven ability to generate pipeline and win new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of meeting or exceeding sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling connectivity, network infrastructure or data centre solutions to Enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial mindset, with the drive to identify opportunities and develop new relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, negotiation and relationship-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex sales cycles and multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who is comfortable prospecting and building opportunities from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of the European Telecoms and Enterprise connectivity market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this position is of interest but you don’t think you meet all of the criteria listed, please consider applying still. euNetworks looks to recruit people with the right attitude, potential and ambition and for the right candidate, we will provide further training and support to enable you to develop in the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer you?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At euNetworks we invest in our people by offering a range of benefits and development opportunities designed to support your professional growth and personal wellbeing. Employees have access to a comprehensive wellbeing programme that promotes mental health and also recognises the importance of work-life balance through initiatives such as a dedicated birthday day off and “give back” days to support volunteering activities. euNetworks’ bonus scheme is linked to both individual contribution and overall company performance with opportunity to overachieve in both areas. In addition, euNetworks operates a flexible hybrid working policy, enabling employees to balance in-office collaboration with remote work, fostering productivity, autonomy and a positive employee experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Family Friendly Policy delivers enhanced and inclusive parental benefits that can viewed &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1yM2VvLsByNiULKnRX9pIksCK0GI6FmO2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=105588911760161167743&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Insurances, pensions, leave and additional enhancements are modelled to work with local country provisions, please email &lt;a ---------- for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our company values drive our behaviour and form the basis of how we operate our business. We work as a team promoting a culture of collaboration, trust and respect where every individual is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and commit to providing each individual with the support, continued learning and the tools to achieve their goals and an environment in which they can thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to make the hiring process equitable and accessible for all. Providing candidates with the opportunity to be their true selves and explore how you might thrive at euNetworks. We are a recognised Disability Confident employer and will make provisions where possible to support you through the interview process, if you require any reasonable accommodation through the selection process, please let your Talent Partner know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we do?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;euNetworks is a pan-European provider of bandwidth infrastructure services and a vital enabler of Cloud and AI adoption. We’re the leading connectivity partner for data centre companies and their customers in Europe, directly connecting over 600 data centres today. We own and operate 18 metropolitan city networks connected with a high capacity intercity backbone covering 53 cities in 17 countries. A leading provider of cloud connectivity, we&amp;nbsp;directly connect to all major cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Sales  London

Senior Business Development Associate &lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Business Development Associate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a Nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Business Development Associates bring ideas, initiatives, and activities that help grow our business day in and day out. They join, support, and collaborate with teams focused on specific opportunities, ensuring that the pursuit of new business is rigorous, disciplined, and ethical. They collaborate closely to craft strategies and plans and set the standard for creative excellence in business development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IDEO London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a global design consultancy where curiosity, empathy, and solving complex challenges drive us. For over 40 years, we&#39;ve partnered with clients to innovate in healthcare, mobility, education, retail, and beyond. Here, every challenge is a chance to grow, connect, and create impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why is this role important for IDEO&#39;s work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business Development is at the heart of connecting IDEO&#39;s creative capabilities with the people and organisations who need them. It&#39;s about more than winning new work. It&#39;s about understanding our clients&#39; challenges, building trusted relationships, and helping shape opportunities where human-centred design can make a meaningful difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Once Here You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize your time to collaborate and support the London Studio in landing project work - with new and returning clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run pipeline meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an IDEO ambassador and be the first touch point for new potential clients, ensuring a positive initial experience with IDEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage opportunity qualification, owning continuity of the BD process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involve internal leadership and designers as needed for boosts and to help determine strategic fit, frame opportunities, scope programs and articulate next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull in director-level support as needed for advocating for client needs and negotiation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finalize pitch decks, learn the industries of our client leads by conducting research and editing proposal decks, and brainstorm client deliverable options and consulting solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct client due diligence to help BD teams get smart and prepare for calls, creating intelligent discussion guides that help us start to build a relationship with potential clients from Day One.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and communicate market trends and themes to teams on a monthly basis that can be used to help shape our thinking and offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REPORTING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track quarterly goals pertaining to recognized revenue, monthly profit and yield marks, time to close, conversion rate, qualification rate, and win rate KPIs within the London Hub. Report back in the pipeline meetings, looking for ways to engage the team in the information and how they need to apply it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be familiar with metrics that point towards the health of the business and be able to assist with ad-hoc reporting needs as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare a monthly summary of insights and thought leadership (from IDEO and beyond), including how it applies to day-to-day business, to share with key clients as a value add.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DATA INTEGRITY&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Director/Enterprise team to ensure the CRM system is kept up to date, including our pipeline and pre-pipeline in Hubspot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that relevant documents related to BD are being stored and filed accordingly in the BD section of Google Drive (not on personal drives or Slack!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appropriately loop in Legal, Marketing, Finance, and other functions as needed to progress an ongoing BD process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain lists in Hubspot and LinkedIn Sales Navigator: who are our key clients, our lapsed clients, our warm contacts, the cold contacts we want to reach? Who’s engaging with our newsletters, with our LinkedIn, etc? Provide recommendations on how we might reach out to these folks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROGRAM MANAGEMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise project management tactical skills by effectively steering the BD process for new and existing work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and take action on the business development process and client needs based on what we’re hearing and seeing in the pipeline meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate meetings with potential leads, ensure prompt and adequate follow-ups, manage legal agreement workflows, coordinate proposal research across teams, and ensure continual progress to meet client deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team balance meeting the needs of existing clientele with prioritizing time for proactive outreach to land new clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and project manage lead generation activities, such as BD-specific mailers to LON Hub mailing lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support account planning activities to drive a proactive, consistent approach to client investment and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the deployment of the right expertise and experience from within the hub team towards client pursuits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMMUNICATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate persuasive and effective communication and presentation skills along with the confidence to command a room for the client and network-building meetings or events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to providing excellent team and client communication and collaboration that shows an understanding of leading with empathy, openness, and curiosity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower other team members to consistently gather and share inspiration, work, and learnings with teams and clients. This should come through leading by example as well as having a knowledge management system where folks can exchange and store content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen existing assets and develop new ones in collaboration with subject matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with LON Hub Marketing to stay abreast of competitors and any impact that industry and economic changes and movements might have on our go to market positioning and offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NETWORK BUILDING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate knowledge of the different approaches across each of our three offer sets, and understand the different areas of expertise of our design disciplines to confidently speak to our capabilities in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build cross-discipline relationships across IDEO in order to effectively help generate and capture written, verbal and visual input from IDEO leadership and design teams to potential client leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate your internal networks as well as you professional networks virtually on social media channels and live at education and industry-related associations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support top-of-funnel growth activity including working with the Executive Director of Growth, Marketing and portfolio teams to translate targeting priorities into actionable prospect audiences and lists for campaigns, events, roadshows and other market-facing activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPLORE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen your foundational BD skills and capabilities, using your learning budget intentionally to build on growth opportunities identified with your business lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain an understanding of GenAI and how it can support and improve the BD process, from generating client intelligence to scoring our RFP responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support special projects as needed and provide support on other processes and projects outside the immediate area of responsibilities as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with internal programs and initiatives to improve organizational BD efforts, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an active member of the London community, coming into the office as needed, playing a role in our core rituals, such as Tuesday Morning Meetings, participating in SASU, and attending Hub gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 3-5 years of relevant experience in client relationship management and business development, preferably within a creative environment and/or design consultancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management skills with proven ability to prioritize tasks, keep momentum and develop timelines, involve and engage stakeholders, and maintain empathy for both internal and client teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to create and deliver presentations, proposals, and other assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data literacy: fluent in G-suite (slides, docs, and sheets), Workday, CRM, and translating quantitative outputs into actionable qualitative insights for the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and communication skills to effectively and efficiently bridge between IDEO and its clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct and synthesize research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to Detail: Demonstrates concern for the details and their impact on the larger picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a wide range of market analysis tools, data sets, and benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort determining next steps in ambiguous situations with limited direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to pitch in on tasks, big or small. Volunteer and helper mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to collaborate across various design disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take chances without being afraid to fail and learn along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insatiable curiosity to learn more about businesses, industries, markets, and what drives them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MINDSET&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ground in Self-Awareness: Reflect on your biases and lenses to be more inclusive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show Curiosity: Question accepted norms to make room to learn from more diverse voices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean into Vulnerability: Build trust by being open.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask for and give consistent and timely feedback on personal performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be optimistic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embrace ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talk Less, Do more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make others successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does IDEO offer you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation and creativity:&lt;/strong&gt; Dive into a variety of projects from creating breakthrough digital products and experiences, to designing new customer interactions, to building innovation capabilities – working alongside talented individuals across disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning and growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Whether it’s strengthening your project leadership, deepening your interaction design craft or exploring new technologies, we’re here to support your journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community and well-being:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaboration and community are central to what we do. We foster moments for creativity, connection, and reflection, respecting the need for work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Projects with purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; We partner with clients to use design as a means of realising their purpose and making a positive impact. We work &#39;upstream,&#39; from defining the problem, designing possible solutions, and exploring what, why and how they might be brought to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£55,000 - 60,000 GBP, depending on experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some Previous Projects To Check Out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To get a flavour of the work we do in London, take a look at these case studies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/works/sage&quot;&gt;Climate action for SMBs&lt;/a&gt; – Designing a strategy and experience to help Sage’s SMB customers transition to net zero.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/case-study/femsa&quot;&gt;Redefining retail with FEMSA&lt;/a&gt; – Designing Spin Premia, a digital loyalty experience connecting everyday shopping at OXXO with rewards and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/works/h-and-m&quot;&gt;Sustainable packaging system&lt;/a&gt; – Helping H&amp;amp;M increase their sustainability and growth, by designing and scaling a universal packaging system for all of their brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IDEO, we are committed to the work of advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion within our organisation and in the world. Our purpose of having disproportionate, world-changing impact through design is directly connected to our ability to bring many different perspectives to the table. This applies to our candidates, the people we hire, the clients and customers we serve, and the communities we learn from in our research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a human-centred organisation, we are committed to working with and designing for people of every race, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, socio-economic status, physical ability or attribute, religion, national origin, or political belief. We recognize that this commitment requires ongoing work and sustained attention, as well as adaptation to new insights and best practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Requirements And Instructions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you identify with our values, are excited about great design, and would like to contribute to our community, we would love to see your CV, a cover letter and examples of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Business Development  London

Account Manager, Client Development & Renewals &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Our Purpose&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SentinelOne, we are driven by a clear purpose: to give the advantage to those who secure our future. As AI reshapes how organizations build, operate, and innovate, the responsibility to protect them becomes more critical than ever. When you join SentinelOne, your work helps protect global enterprises, critical infrastructure, and the technologies shaping tomorrow. If you are motivated by meaningful challenges and want your impact to be real, measurable, and global, you will find purpose here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SentinelOne is a company at the intersection of AI and security, pioneering a new operating model for cybersecurity. Our AI-native platform unifies protection across endpoint, cloud, identity, data, and AI systems to deliver autonomous detection and response with clarity and speed. By combining real-time analytics, intelligent automation, and a unified data foundation, we reduce noise, simplify complexity, and empower security teams to focus on what truly matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams are builders, problem-solvers, and innovators committed to shaping the future of security. If you are excited to solve hard problems alongside talented, mission-driven people, we invite you to help us build a safer future for humanity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Are We Looking For?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who are relentlessly curious and committed to continuous learning. AI is reshaping every function across our business, and we enable every team member, regardless of role or level, to build fluency in AI tools and concepts. Those who thrive here actively seek out new solutions, experiment thoughtfully, and apply what they learn to drive better, faster, smarter outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As an Account Manager, Client Development &amp;amp; Renewals, you will own a book of existing customer accounts and drive both renewal retention and expansion revenue within them. This is a growth-first role where renewal is the floor, not the goal: you will protect the base by keeping renewals healthy and on time, and grow it by uncovering whitespace, running consultative upsell and cross-sell conversations, and turning satisfied customers into expanding ones. Working closely with Account Executives, Customer Success Managers, and Sales Engineers, you will build account plans and get ahead of risk before it reaches the forecast. If you are driven to outgrow a base you know well, own your numbers, and earn a path to strategic accounts or AE-track roles through expansion results, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Will You Do?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Primary responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of existing accounts carrying a dual quota of renewal retention and expansion bookings, identifying whitespace across the SentinelOne portfolio and leading consultative upsell and cross-sell conversations built around customer use cases and outcomes rather than just quotes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot expansion triggers early, such as new use cases, organizational growth, underutilized licenses, and competitive displacement openings, and build repeatable account plans with your CSM and SE partners that map multi-year growth rather than just the next renewal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage renewals end to end, from early quoting and multi-threading through negotiation and on-time close, handling commercial negotiations including multi-year commitments and keeping timelines definitive and forecasts predictable across your book.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify churn and downgrade risk early by monitoring deployment health, usage, support signals, and sentiment, running save motions on at-risk accounts with CSM, Support, and leadership, and getting ahead of overdeployment and downgrade exposure before it hits the renewal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own an accurate, transparent forecast across renewal and expansion pipeline, keep Salesforce and CPQ tools current, and partner with CSMs, AEs, SEs, and Channel/MSSP partners on account coverage and growth while bringing the customer’s voice back to Product and the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Skills and Knowledge Will You Bring?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years in renewals, account management, or a customer-facing sales role with upsell and cross-sell closing experience, ideally in SaaS or cybersecurity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hitting or beating quota, including driving net revenue retention above 100% on your own book, with expansion outpacing churn rather than renewal completion alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience running consultative upsell and cross-sell motions, identifying and closing whitespace within an existing customer base, and negotiating confidently with senior and economic buyers across multi-stakeholder conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A risk-aware instinct for spotting early signals of churn or downgrade, combined with strong forecasting discipline, CRM hygiene, and hands-on experience with Salesforce and CPQ or quoting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and organizational skills, curiosity about customer use cases and the product, and a habit of opening expansion conversations unprompted, with comfort in a fast-paced, high-growth environment. Exposure to Channel/MSSP or 2-tier GTM models is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why SentinelOne?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is redefining how the world operates and rewriting the rules of security in real time, and SentinelOne was built for this moment. From day one, we architected an AI-native platform designed to operate at machine speed, not as an add-on to legacy systems but as the foundation itself. If you want to build where innovation and impact move together, this is that place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our Sentinels with comprehensive, competitive benefits designed to support you and your family:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity &amp;amp; Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive leave benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gender-neutral parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insurance &amp;amp; Financial Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical and insurance benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Perks &amp;amp; Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global home office allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile phone reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-from-home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
