Junior Product Manager – IT Fulfillment &lt;h6&gt;Every order a Suitsupply customer places, online, in a store, or through customer service, has to be captured, understood and carried all the way through to delivery or return. As Junior Product Manager for IT Fulfillment, you will help build and improve the services that make that happen: the order flows, data and interfaces that connect our webstore, our stores, our warehouses and our customer service teams.&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;You will work in a small team inside the IT Fulfillment domain, alongside the Group Product Manager and our own engineers. The Group Product Manager shapes the functional direction with the business and sets priorities; together you turn it into clear requirements, well-defined tickets and working software, built with engineers and AI agents. This is a technical product role: we build our own services, so you will spend your time in data models, interfaces and requirements rather than managing a vendor’s roadmap. You start close to delivery, with support while you learn the domain, and grow into owning more of the roadmap.&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn mapped-out functional flows into clear, buildable work: technical requirements, acceptance criteria and user stories that engineers and AI agents can pick up without coming back with questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the detail as both product manager and business analyst: the data model, the way systems talk to each other, and the edge cases nobody thought of yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break large changes into chunks that can be built, tested and released safely, and keep the backlog in a state where work can start at any moment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineers day to day in refinement, planning, reviews and releases, and use our AI tooling to draft, structure and pressure-test the work before it reaches them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design our order data and interfaces so that AI agents can read, reason over and act on them as reliably as our own systems do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create visibility across the end-to-end fulfillment journey, so anyone from a customer service agent to a supply chain lead can see where an order is and what happened to it, and turn that into measures the business trusts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on discovery for smaller and mid-sized roadmap items as your domain knowledge builds: the options, the trade-offs and the recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business analysis experience: 2+ years of hands-on experience as a Business Analyst or Product Owner. You have written functional and technical specifications, worked directly with developers, and been accountable for the detail being right. The analysis craft is what we are hiring for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain experience: That experience is in fulfillment, order management, supply chain, e-commerce or retail operations. You know what an order, a shipment, an allocation and a return actually are, and what it costs operationally when one goes wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eye for detail: You chase the last open question rather than leaving it for someone else to find in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native mindset: You already work with tools like Claude and Cursor every day to analyse, draft, prototype and check your own thinking, and you know what to hand over and what to validate yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency: You can hold your own in a technical conversation without being an engineer, and you say “I don’t understand that yet” rather than guessing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: You are a clear writer who asks the uncomfortable question early rather than the polite one late.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Business, Technology, or a related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomy: We empower you to take ownership, make meaningful decisions, and drive impact close to our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth: You will develop within a high-performance digital product environment, increasing your business impact and decision scope over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate Social Responsibility: Our commitment to sustainability and ethical business is unwavering. We work exclusively with suppliers who uphold the highest standards, in alignment with the International Labour Organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Style: Immerse yourself in a world of beautifully crafted, high-quality products, and enjoy a 40% discount on Suitsupply products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: We offer a competitive salary based on relevant skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a> IT Development  Amsterdam

Working Student - LLM Quantization & Inference Performance &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tensordyne (formerly Recogni)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is transforming our world. It can perform cognitive functions that previously only humans could do, such as perceiving interactions across different modalities and environments - with the ability to quickly learn and then solve complex problems. Tensordyne is an AI system solution company that builds very high-performance, low-power generative AI inference systems. Our mission, through the creation of custom silicon, hardware and software, is to enable multimodal Generative AI inference acceleration at scale, with safe, sustainable, high-performance systems for our hyperscaler and neocloud data center customers. We are at the leading edge of advancing the latest research and product improvements for generative Al inference solutions that will make Al even more advantageous for compelling new generative AI applications.Tensordyne is a well funded, fast-paced startup company with headquarters in both Sunnyvale, CA, and Munich, Germany. We also have many talented team members working remotely across North America and Europe. We take care of our people and their families with comprehensive benefits, competitive compensation, flexible spending options, and recognition programs, because building category-defining technology starts with a healthy, supported team. Come join us as we shape the future of multimodal generative artificial intelligence!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How much numerical precision does an LLM need, and where in the model architecture does it matter most? When does quantization improve runtime, and what does it cost in model quality?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;motivated working student&lt;/strong&gt; to help turn these questions into experiments and experiments into maintainable code. You’ll explore optimization methods and build reusable evaluation tooling. You’ll work closely with our quantization, compiler, and runtime engineers, and your findings will directly influence how we optimize models for Tensordyne hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model quality evaluation:&lt;/strong&gt; Measure how low-precision computation affects performance on coding and reasoning benchmarks. Diagnose where quantization has the greatest impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quantization research:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement and compare post-training quantization methods to improve inference efficiency while preserving task accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build reproducible tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Automate evaluations, track configurations and results, and make experiments accessible to engineers and AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure runtime performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Characterize latency, throughput, and memory usage to understand bottlenecks under different deployment scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A first project could involve exploring the quality–performance Pareto frontier of a Qwen or LlaMa model. You’ll experiment with 16-bit, 8-bit, and 4-bit quantization configurations to find the best runtime-quality tradeoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current enrollment in Computer Science, Mathematics, Electrical Engineering, Machine Learning, or a related master’s degree program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python and PyTorch skills, including the ability to understand and modify model implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective use of AI coding tools and critical review of their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An experimental mindset: you can formulate hypotheses, design comparisons, and draw careful conclusions from noisy results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and the ability to present experimental findings and technical tradeoffs to the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong pluses:&lt;/strong&gt; experience with quantization, LLM evaluation, performance profiling, or inference optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for you if you &lt;strong&gt;thrive on responsibility, learn quickly, and are naturally proactive&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a deep-tech team building the next generation of AI inference systems. Put your university knowledge into practice with leading open-source LLMs, deepen your understanding of quantization and inference optimization, and build skills in experimental design, software engineering, and AI coding tools. You’ll own a focused project, receive close mentorship from experienced engineers, and have room to explore ideas that shape our optimization methods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tensordyne&#39;s culture was built on the following values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put people first. We only succeed when our people succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ethics and integrity always. Be open, honest, and respectful of everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think Big. Be ambitious and have audacious goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aim for excellence. Quality and excellence count in everything we do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own it and get it done. Results matter!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make each person better together than they would be as an individual.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embrace each other’s differences, and embrace that there will be differences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tensordyne is an equal opportunity employer. We believe diverse teams are better equipped to solve complex problems and build exceptional technology. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, gender identity or expression, marital status, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, race, religion, pregnancy, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note to recruitment agencies: Please do not contact Tensordyne employees or leaders regarding this role. We do not accept unsolicited agency resumes and are not responsible for fees associated with unsolicited submissions.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  Munich

Strategic Alliances Director, France &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Anaplan, we are a team of innovators focused on optimizing business decision-making through our leading AI-infused scenario planning and analysis platform so our customers can outpace their competition and the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What unites Anaplanners across teams and geographies is our collective commitment to our customers’ success and to our Winning Culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Our customers rank among the who’s who in the Fortune 50. Coca-Cola, LinkedIn, Adobe, LVMH and Bayer are just a few of the 2,400+ global companies who rely on our best-in-class platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Our Winning Culture is the engine that drives our teams of innovators. We champion diversity of thought and ideas, we behave like leaders regardless of title, we are committed to achieving ambitious goals, and we love celebrating&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;our wins – big and small.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supported by operating principles of being strategy-led, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anaplan.com/careers/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt;-based and disciplined in execution, you’ll be inspired, connected, developed and rewarded here. Everything that makes you unique is welcome; join us and let’s build what’s next - together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a pivotal, high-impact opportunity to become the architect of Anaplan&#39;s partner-led growth across the France market.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anaplan is seeking an experienced Strategic Alliances Director to lead our partner ecosystem in France. This role will focus on partner recruitment, driving demand generation, increasing awareness, and enabling our trusted partners to successfully market and deliver Anaplan solutions. You will act as the primary liaison between Anaplan and our partners, helping them expand their skill sets, certifications, market reach and drive joint market demand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role, You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a comprehensive partner engagement strategy to promote Anaplan’s offerings across France.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive demand generation initiatives collaboratively with partners and internal teams to ensure pipeline growth and attainment of joint revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise awareness of Anaplan’s solutions through enablement programs, workshops, and targeted communications for partner sales and delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partner readiness with the partner success team by defining and enforcing prerequisites, including certifications, solution knowledge, and delivery capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with marketing to create relevant content and campaigns tailored to partner audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor partner performance and provide feedback, support, and strategic guidance to maximise partner contribution and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with sales, product, and customer success teams to align partner activities with overall business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise and relevant regional experience in alliance management or partnership development within technology or related sectors, often supported by an advanced degree in business or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in software sales and revenue growth through strategic alliances, with experience in developing and managing partnerships with Global System Integrators, Cloud providers, and other key partners at a regional or global level.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills including the ability to lead alliances and channels, develop and execute go-to-market (GTM) strategies, and drive partner sales and engagement in complex, matrix organisations.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, negotiation, and executive presentation skills with the ability to influence diverse stakeholders and foster collaborative relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in operational and strategic sales planning, partner business planning, marketing plans, and revenue-driving program execution, coupled with commercial acumen and analytical skills.​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and English is required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultural intelligence and sensitivity to effectively navigate diverse markets, business customs, and regulatory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking and business acumen to identify growth opportunities, anticipate market trends, and align alliance strategies with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience and adaptability to thrive in dynamic, fast-paced technology markets and manage complexities related to emerging technologies and evolving partner ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-centric mindset focused on driving partner-enabled customer success and delivering measurable business outcomes through alliances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Anaplan or similar cloud-based enterprise planning platforms is advantageous but not mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us at Anaplan to drive innovation through our partner network and shape the future of connected planning!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity, Equity, Inclusion and Belonging (DEIB) &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe attracting and retaining the best talent and fostering an inclusive culture strengthens our business. DEIB improves our workforce, enhances trust with our partners and customers, and drives business success. Build your career in a place where diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging aren’t just words on paper – this is what drives our innovation, it’s how we connect, and it contributes to what makes us a market leader. We believe in a hiring and working environment where all people are respected and valued, regardless of gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, ethnicity, age, neurodiversity, disability status, citizenship, or any other aspect which makes people unique. We hire you for who you are, and we want you to bring your authentic self to work every day! &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive equitable benefits and all privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraud Recruitment Disclaimer&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It has come to our attention that fraudulent and fictitious job opportunities are being circulated on the Internet. Prospective candidates are being contacted by certain individuals, mainly through telephone calls, emails and correspondence, claiming they are representatives of Anaplan. The main purpose of these correspondences and announcements is to obtain privileged information from individuals.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anaplan does not: &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend offers to candidates without an extensive interview process with a member of our recruitment team and a hiring manager via video or in person.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Send job offers via email. All offers are first extended verbally by a member of our internal recruitment team whenever possible and then followed up via written communication. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All emails from Anaplan would come from an ----- email address. Should you have any doubts about the authenticity of an email, letter or telephone communication purportedly from, for, or on behalf of Anaplan, please send an email to ----- before taking any further action in relation to the correspondence.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW36347262 BCX0&quot;&gt;Privacy &amp;amp; AI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW36347262 BCX0&quot;&gt; Notice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;andidate data processed during our recruitment activities is handled &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;in accordance with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt; our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anaplan.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. This may include the use of artificial intelligence or automated tools to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;assist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt; our team in evaluating qualifications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
